Well, opinions differ widely on this. Lots of long-time players in this
newsgroup think that *every* character should be played as if you were
playing yourself. Hence, no character they play will take potential mortal
risks.

These players only quaff or dip if they really have to, and even then,
very reluctantly. They usually only do it with advanced characters as
well, because they at least have a chance of survival if things go wrong.

Also, your character has to be capable of removing curses, in case items
in your inventory gets cursed. Read Ellora's story about quaffing from
fountains with an advanced character:

http://roguelikes.sauceforge.net/pub/www/nethack/stories/ (part 32)

and you'll understand why even well-equipped, high-level characters should
be very careful to quaff from or dip into fountains.

